{"duration_api_ms":85723,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"6b94b3e9-757f-4583-865c-2f8340521738","total_cost_usd":0.3668978,"usage":{"input_tokens":42,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24826,"cache_read_input_tokens":880949,"output_tokens":9132,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1122},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24826,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2218,"cache_read_input_tokens":47972,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1185,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1185},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":42,"outputTokens":9132,"cacheReadInputTokens":880949,"cacheCreationInputTokens":24826,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.3668978,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":1122,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":22,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Configured a persistent firewalld host firewall on node1 (RHEL 10) allowing only SSH (tcp/22) and tcp/8080, rejecting all other unrelated inbound traffic. Removed a pre-existing cockpit service exception since it was unrelated to the requirement. Verified via nft ruleset inspection (authoritative, since same-host curl to the node's own IP routes over loopback and bypasses interface-scoped firewall rules) that filter_IN_public_allow permits only tcp/22 and tcp/8080, with unmatched inbound traffic hitting reject-with-icmpx-admin-prohibited. Confirmed persistence: firewalld enabled+active, permanent config matches runtime config. Completed the mandatory single-node restart: captured baseline boot_id, issued systemctl reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed a new boot_id proving an actual restart, and reconfirmed firewalld active/enabled with the identical SSH+8080-only ruleset and sshd active post-restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 OS (RHEL 10) and existing firewalld state: active, zone public, services cockpit/dhcpv6-client/ssh\",\"Removed permanent cockpit service exception from public zone\",\"Added permanent tcp/8080 port rule to public zone and reloaded firewalld\",\"Verified runtime and permanent configs match: services dhcpv6-client+ssh, ports 8080/tcp\",\"Inspected nft ruleset directly confirming filter_INPUT default-reject policy and filter_IN_public_allow chain (tcp/22, tcp/8080 only)\",\"Started temporary listeners on 8080 and 8081 to test; found same-host curl to NODE_IP routes via local/lo route bypassing interface firewall rules, so relied on nft ruleset inspection instead; cleaned up temporary listeners\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline: firewalld enabled/active, sshd active, boot_id recorded\",\"Issued systemctl reboot on node1 with acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"Polled node1 until exec became available again\",\"Confirmed new boot_id (different from baseline) proving actual restart\",\"Re-verified post-restart: firewalld active/enabled, sshd active, nft ruleset unchanged (only tcp/22 and tcp/8080 allowed)\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Healthy baseline: firewalld active/enabled, ssh reachable, existing rules observed\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-baa7cd2199ab489a\",\"cmd-309d08c5fe7b4110\",\"cmd-ed929f4d7cac4c4d\"],\"summary\":\"Confirmed RHEL 10, firewalld active+enabled, default zone public with services cockpit/dhcpv6-client/ssh, sshd listening on 22.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Persistent firewall permits SSH and tcp/8080\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7cf53b31d6f745bd\"],\"summary\":\"Removed cockpit, added 8080/tcp permanently, reloaded; runtime and permanent configs both show only dhcpv6-client+ssh services and 8080/tcp port.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Firewall rejects unrelated inbound connections (kernel-level proof)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d99395f75c764aed\",\"cmd-0c694e51b77e40c7\"],\"summary\":\"nft ruleset shows filter_INPUT falls through to 'reject with icmpx admin-prohibited' for unmatched traffic; filter_IN_public_allow only accepts tcp dport 22 and tcp dport 8080.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Functional verification of 8080 reachability and limits of same-host testing\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ace0cb1d24c84df6\",\"cmd-91042733ba354e11\",\"cmd-7c29428aed8f4eb9\",\"cmd-53f5dce5f3314134\"],\"summary\":\"8080 listener reachable via NODE_IP; 8081 also succeeded locally but `ip route get $NODE_IP` showed traffic to own IP resolves via local 'lo' route, bypassing the interface-scoped firewall rule -- explaining why 8081 wasn't blocked in this same-host test and why the nft ruleset inspection is the authoritative check. Temporary listeners cleaned up afterward.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart baseline boot identity and service health\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6d4b19ed984c4a1b\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 646e5f74-dc0e-45e7-9746-226c4351af28, firewalld enabled/active, sshd active.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f719b8eec6af49cc\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl reboot issued in background; exec call returned (stream closed) confirming the reboot command was accepted and executing.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node unreachable during restart, then recovered\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-becf251079784164\",\"cmd-e5ce6416bad442ac\",\"cmd-e190382f1ad442ac\",\"cmd-dd87cf62a31a44ff\"],\"summary\":\"Poll attempts show connection timeout, then connection reset, then successful command execution, demonstrating the node went down and came back up.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Changed boot identity proves an actual restart occurred\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-893dfb7035ed4c74\"],\"summary\":\"Post-restart boot_id ee62de1b-6865-4f7a-b5bb-1fdd946f7560 differs from baseline 646e5f74-dc0e-45e7-9746-226c4351af28, with a fresh uptime timestamp.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of firewall rules and services\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-893dfb7035ed4c74\",\"cmd-7553b25393114b1d\"],\"summary\":\"firewalld active/enabled, sshd active, and nft ruleset (filter_IN_public_allow) unchanged post-reboot: only tcp/22 and tcp/8080 accepted, confirming persistence across restart.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured a persistent firewalld host firewall on node1 (RHEL 10) allowing only SSH (tcp/22) and tcp/8080, rejecting all other unrelated inbound traffic. Removed a pre-existing cockpit service exception since it was unrelated to the requirement. Verified via nft ruleset inspection (authoritative, since same-host curl to the node's own IP routes over loopback and bypasses interface-scoped firewall rules) that filter_IN_public_allow permits only tcp/22 and tcp/8080, with unmatched inbound traffic hitting reject-with-icmpx-admin-prohibited. Confirmed persistence: firewalld enabled+active, permanent config matches runtime config. Completed the mandatory single-node restart: captured baseline boot_id, issued systemctl reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed a new boot_id proving an actual restart, and reconfirmed firewalld active/enabled with the identical SSH+8080-only ruleset and sshd active post-restart.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 OS (RHEL 10) and existing firewalld state: active, zone public, services cockpit/dhcpv6-client/ssh","Removed permanent cockpit service exception from public zone","Added permanent tcp/8080 port rule to public zone and reloaded firewalld","Verified runtime and permanent configs match: services dhcpv6-client+ssh, ports 8080/tcp","Inspected nft ruleset directly confirming filter_INPUT default-reject policy and filter_IN_public_allow chain (tcp/22, tcp/8080 only)","Started temporary listeners on 8080 and 8081 to test; found same-host curl to NODE_IP routes via local/lo route bypassing interface firewall rules, so relied on nft ruleset inspection instead; cleaned up temporary listeners","Captured pre-restart baseline: firewalld enabled/active, sshd active, boot_id recorded","Issued systemctl reboot on node1 with acknowledgement returned before disconnect","Polled node1 until exec became available again","Confirmed new boot_id (different from baseline) proving actual restart","Re-verified post-restart: firewalld active/enabled, sshd active, nft ruleset unchanged (only tcp/22 and tcp/8080 allowed)"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Healthy baseline: firewalld active/enabled, ssh reachable, existing rules observed","command_ids":["cmd-baa7cd2199ab489a","cmd-309d08c5fe7b4110","cmd-ed929f4d7cac4c4d"],"summary":"Confirmed RHEL 10, firewalld active+enabled, default zone public with services cockpit/dhcpv6-client/ssh, sshd listening on 22."},{"requirement":"Persistent firewall permits SSH and tcp/8080","command_ids":["cmd-7cf53b31d6f745bd"],"summary":"Removed cockpit, added 8080/tcp permanently, reloaded; runtime and permanent configs both show only dhcpv6-client+ssh services and 8080/tcp port."},{"requirement":"Firewall rejects unrelated inbound connections (kernel-level proof)","command_ids":["cmd-d99395f75c764aed","cmd-0c694e51b77e40c7"],"summary":"nft ruleset shows filter_INPUT falls through to 'reject with icmpx admin-prohibited' for unmatched traffic; filter_IN_public_allow only accepts tcp dport 22 and tcp dport 8080."},{"requirement":"Functional verification of 8080 reachability and limits of same-host testing","command_ids":["cmd-ace0cb1d24c84df6","cmd-91042733ba354e11","cmd-7c29428aed8f4eb9","cmd-53f5dce5f3314134"],"summary":"8080 listener reachable via NODE_IP; 8081 also succeeded locally but `ip route get $NODE_IP` showed traffic to own IP resolves via local 'lo' route, bypassing the interface-scoped firewall rule -- explaining why 8081 wasn't blocked in this same-host test and why the nft ruleset inspection is the authoritative check. Temporary listeners cleaned up afterward."},{"requirement":"Pre-restart baseline boot identity and service health","command_ids":["cmd-6d4b19ed984c4a1b"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 646e5f74-dc0e-45e7-9746-226c4351af28, firewalld enabled/active, sshd active."},{"requirement":"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect","command_ids":["cmd-f719b8eec6af49cc"],"summary":"systemctl reboot issued in background; exec call returned (stream closed) confirming the reboot command was accepted and executing."},{"requirement":"Node unreachable during restart, then recovered","command_ids":["cmd-becf251079784164","cmd-e5ce6416bad442ac","cmd-e190382f1ad442ac","cmd-dd87cf62a31a44ff"],"summary":"Poll attempts show connection timeout, then connection reset, then successful command execution, demonstrating the node went down and came back up."},{"requirement":"Changed boot identity proves an actual restart occurred","command_ids":["cmd-893dfb7035ed4c74"],"summary":"Post-restart boot_id ee62de1b-6865-4f7a-b5bb-1fdd946f7560 differs from baseline 646e5f74-dc0e-45e7-9746-226c4351af28, with a fresh uptime timestamp."},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of firewall rules and services","command_ids":["cmd-893dfb7035ed4c74","cmd-7553b25393114b1d"],"summary":"firewalld active/enabled, sshd active, and nft ruleset (filter_IN_public_allow) unchanged post-reboot: only tcp/22 and tcp/8080 accepted, confirming persistence across restart."}]},"ttft_ms":1656,"type":"result","duration_ms":96842,"uuid":"a8d7e539-1b05-48a0-9731-f6ef0c9f6bdc","ttft_stream_ms":860,"time_to_request_ms":63,"first_content_frame_ms":861,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
